Read (bounded): conference/model_v2/SCIENTIFIC_LOCK.md; conference/model_v2/trans_intervention.py (API: placements, coords; conventions exon7 last base 70076574, first intron base 70076575); feng/src/feng/titration/gpu_scores.py (existing Pangolin on-target scorer: reuse narrowly, do not import old pre/src); feng/src/feng/gpu/{env.py,checkpoint.py}; feng/scripts/templates/gpu_preemptable.sbatch; feng/src/feng/pangolin_package_seed_provenance.json. GPU env: /home/dashii/orcd/pool/feng-gpu-env (verify its python path; pytest env /home/dashii/orcd/pool/smt-isef-env/bin/python). Genome: ~/orcd/scratch/feng/gencode/v50/GRCh38.primary_assembly.genome.fa(+.fai), GTF same dir. No broad /orcd scans. No heavy GPU/CPU on login node — GPU runs ONLY via sbatch (I will submit the sentinel; you write it).
## Contract
Batched, deterministic, strand-correct Pangolin inference engine: (1) reference scoring of splice-site contexts with caching keyed by (locus, window, model, weights hash); (2) prespecified site x length N-ablation grid (N-mask of ASO footprint windows; lengths from a config list, positions tiled with stride) scoring delta vs reference at splice sites in window; outputs reference_scores/* and ablation_maps/* parquet with columns incl. raw_model_delta (NOT ΔPSI), evidence_class="sequence_ablation_proxy" for every N-masked row; model/weight/source sha256 in parquet metadata + manifest; (3) deterministic sharding, bounded GPU batch size with OOM backoff that never drops records (failed => explicit failure row, never zero), atomic tmp->rename, strict .done manifest, SIGTERM checkpoint + --requeue (ONE owner for requeue, per gpu_preemptable template); (4) no off-target/exon sampling informed by measured outcomes; (5) CPU-vs-GPU tolerance test hook (skip w/o GPU, state reason) and real GPU smoke entry `--smoke` (SMN2 exon7 region, F18 footprint grid) with sbatch jobs/j4_sentinel.sbatch (mit_normal_gpu or preemptable per template, <=15 min).
Scientific invariants: N-mask is a cis-feature sensitivity proxy, not physical ASO occupancy; chromosome coordinates 1-based inclusive internally, convert once at boundary with unit tests (0/1-based, half-open); minus-strand genes reverse-complement correctly; label outputs observed/derived/proxy/etc. per SCIENTIFIC_LOCK. Unit tests CPU-only with a stub scorer where weights unavailable (stub clearly named; never counted as model evidence).
## Acceptance
pytest passes on CPU; write conference/model_v2/ops/briefs/J4_RESULT.md (<=40 lines): files, exact pytest counts, how to run sentinel, open questions. Do not commit.
